# Synapse-Hub Manual QA Rules

1. **ISO/IEC/IEEE 29119-3 12-Column Contract:** All manual test case tables MUST follow the canonical 12-column schema defined in `skills/02-test-design/rbt-manual-testing/SKILL.md` (`TC ID | Module | Risk Level | Test Title | Pre-Condition | Test Steps | Expected Result | Priority | Test Data | Automatable | Auto Type | Tags`), embedding requirement traceability tags (`@REQ-xxx`) inside `Tags` (or optionally inserting a dedicated 13th `REQ ID` column immediately after `TC ID`).
2. **Zero Speculative Language:** NEVER write ambiguous or hedging phrases in Expected Results or Steps (ban: `"HOẶC"`, `"OR"` for unverified behavior, `"tùy backend"`, `"tùy hệ thống"`, `"an toàn"`, `"xử lý hợp lý"`, `"if applicable"`). Every expected result MUST be deterministic and verifiable. <!-- synapse-ignore: VIETNAMESE -->
3. **Mandatory Hard Checkpoints:** When requirements are incomplete or contradictory, STOP at Stage 2 (Ambiguity Q&A Register) and Stage 4 (RTM & High-Level Scenarios) before authoring detailed test cases. Never invent business rules.
4. **On-Demand Field Validation Loading:** For forms/screens with 8 or fewer input fields, query only the matching field types via `agent-qa checklist --fields <list>` instead of loading the entire 24 KB `field_validation_checklist.md`.
5. **Pre-Delivery Linter Gate:** Before finalizing any Markdown test case suite, run `python tools/lint/manual_tc_linter.py <file> [--profile <profile>] [--strict-semantic]` and resolve all blocking violations.
6. **Automation Rule Isolation:** Do NOT apply automation-only invariants (`Clean POM Flat Architecture`, `Smart Waits Only`, Page Object locator checks) to pure Manual QA Markdown artifacts.

